<h3>Before you read: watch this first</h3>
<p>The <em>Manifesto</em> is more readable than Hegel, but it moves fast and assumes familiarity with mid-nineteenth century European politics and economics. This video introduces the key ideas — historical materialism, class struggle, the critique of capitalism — in plain terms before you encounter them in the text. It will give you a framework to hang the details on as you read.</p>
