<h3>By the end of this unit, you should be able to</h3>
<div>
<div>○ &nbsp; Explain Marx’s account of historical materialism and how it differs from Hegel’s idealism</div>
<div>○ &nbsp; Describe the relationship between the bourgeoisie and the proletariat as Marx and Engels define it</div>
<div>○ &nbsp; Explain what Marx means by the abolition of private property, and how he distinguishes it from the abolition of personal property</div>
<div>○ &nbsp; Identify the three types of socialism Marx critiques in Part 3 of the <em>Manifesto</em> and explain his objection to each</div>
<div>○ &nbsp; Explain the concept of alienated labor and its role in Marx’s critique of capitalism</div>
<div>○ &nbsp; Define false consciousness and explain why it functions as a structural form of self-deception</div>
<div>○ &nbsp; Evaluate at least one of Marx’s central claims, identifying both its philosophical strengths and its problems</div>
</div>
